research/audit/wave3-judge-adjudications.jsonl-78-{"id":"thm-countable-union-of-countable","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","context_sha256":"0b4c79538e3d79a8f5ca3ef6d1c11f30761eb2fac3b1b76bf404afc87507cc4c","item_sha256":"5c980731792c3ecaecf2e6e0d7ee480e6eea160f908d4d2182e8192397dc76bd","outcome":"confirmed_nonfatal","adjudicator":"audit-alpha (claude-opus-5)","at":"2026-08-04","note":"Terra is right that \"Each A_n has such surjections\" is false when A_n is empty. The proof's own step 2.1 handles that case explicitly and visibly (\"for n not in J put S_n := S_{n_0}\"), and step 1.2 defines J as the set of nonempty indices, so the explanatory sentence is contradicted by the proof one screen below rather than relied on. Degenerate empty case, recorded."}
